# Task ledgers live here (docs/tasks/<feature>.md), written at runtime by the team.
#
# RETENTION (set by the 2026-08-13 maintenance pass; apply it, don't re-derive it)
#
# A `status: done` ledger is kept for exactly one reason: its `## Context pack` is
# the only artefact step 2 of the operating recipe can reuse to skip a survey. So
# prune by whether the packed area has MOVED, never by age — a six-month-old pack
# over untouched code is worth more than last week's pack over a rewritten module.
#
# Delete a done ledger when any of these is true:
#   - it has no `## Context pack` at all (nothing to reuse; the build-log entry
#     already carries the decisions and the why);
#   - its pack's load-bearing facts are counterfactual — it freezes a seam, an
#     export list or a file inventory that no longer exists. A counterfactual pack
#     is worse than no pack: it reads as a survey and is a trap.
# Keep it when the pack still describes current code, even if the order is old.
#
# Never delete anything from docs/build-log.md — that file is append-only and
# permanent, and it is what makes deleting a ledger safe. Deleted ledgers also stay
# in git history: `git show <commit>:docs/tasks/<file>` recovers any of them.
#
# Removed 2026-08-18 (321 lines): members-week-selector-removal. The order that
# followed it rewrote app/members/page.tsx (100+ lines -> 73, roster extracted to
# components/RosterTable.tsx), so the pack's load-bearing facts inverted: it says
# the file has NO force-dynamic and DOES await searchParams; both are now false.
# Two of its citations were out of range on measurement. Its one durable lesson
# lives in the load-bearing comment at app/members/page.tsx:7-14 and in the worked
# example in .claude/rules/rendering.md. Six ledgers remain, all with packs that
# still describe current code: the three phase3a/3b/4 packs cover auth, RLS and
# the connection resolver, none of which has changed a byte since 2026-08-13.
#
# Removed 2026-08-13 (all `status: done`, ~1,290 lines): phase1-retire-sheet-sync-
# and-db-switcher, phase2-port-data-layer-to-supabase-postgres (both packs describe
# the libSQL era and a `lib/db.ts` since rewritten twice — phase2's frozen seam even
# specifies the `??` form the rules now forbid); member-links, member-week-edit,
# import-clash-aware-week-tags, member-trend-week-over-week (no context pack; the
# trend ledger's diagnosis describes behaviour its own order replaced).
